Build against the Proxmox crates from their git repositories, and without
libsystemd.

Upstream's .cargo/config.toml replaces crates.io with Debian's packaged
crates (/usr/share/cargo/registry), where Proxmox's own crates (proxmox.git,
pxar.git, pathpatterns.git) come from. FenrirOS has no such registry: this
drops the replacement and patches each Proxmox crate to its git repository
at a fixed commit, the newest at or before proxmox-backup-qemu's
"bump version to 2.0.4" (2026-10-31): proxmox.git b4e7e1e1 (2026-10-30),
pxar.git 091a8a38, pathpatterns.git 5323cbe4. The Cargo.lock in the
recipe's files/ was generated from this configuration.

proxmox-systemd (needed through pbs-datastore) links libsystemd, which
FenrirOS does not have. It is patched to a copy in fenrir/proxmox-systemd/
instead: proxmox.git b4e7e1e1's proxmox-systemd 1.0.1 unchanged, except
- Cargo.toml: the workspace fields it inherits written out;
- src/sys.rs: the six libsystemd functions written in Rust with the same
  signatures and error convention: sd_notify/sd_pid_notify_with_fds send the
  notify datagram to $NOTIFY_SOCKET (nothing, returning 0, when it is unset,
  as under dinit), sd_notify_barrier is 0 without $NOTIFY_SOCKET and ENOSYS
  with it, sd_listen_fds_with_names reads $LISTEN_PID/$LISTEN_FDS/
  $LISTEN_FDNAMES, sd_journal_stream_fd returns a duplicate of stderr (no
  journal), sd_id128_get_machine_app_specific derives the ID from
  /etc/machine-id with HMAC-SHA256 as systemd does.
Only the crates the build uses are patched (and files/Cargo.lock has no
[[patch.unused]] entries): the build is offline against vendored crates, and a
[patch] entry whose crate is not vendored fails with "patch location ... does
not contain packages matching ...".
Written for FenrirOS.

